      "message": "\"EC\" is ambiguous here. In one place it stands for \"Embedded Controller\" and another \"elliptic curve\", right?\n\nSince the constant above (`FP_ELLIPTIC_CURVE_PUBLIC_KEY_POINT_LEN`) doesn\u0027t have the \"ec\" prefix, I would just make this `fp_elliptic_curve_public_key`. We have some examples of not using the `ec` prefix for structs that are not directly used in the request/response:\n\n* https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h;l\u003d7533-7557;drc\u003d7f21c475bb679788a0e04d71780eac8cc78ac5f5\n* https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/include/ec_commands.h;l\u003d7692-7695;drc\u003d7f21c475bb679788a0e04d71780eac8cc78ac5f5\n\nOtherwise this starts to get pretty redundant: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromiumos/platform/ec/+/4477228/86/include/ec_commands.h",
